# Annotating articles

When an article is assigned to you it appears in your **Annotation Queue** in
the sidebar. Click it to open the annotation view.

## Selecting text

Click and drag over any span of text in the abstract or body to open the
annotation editor. The selected sentence is shown for context.

## Creating an entity

After selecting text you can either:

- **Create a new entity** — choose a kind (Enzyme, Bacteria, Strain…), enter a
  preferred name, and confirm.
- **Add to an existing entity** — search for an entity already in the project and
  attach the selected text as an additional mention.

Confirmed entities appear in the **Summary** panel on the right.

## Editing a mention

Click any highlighted span to reopen the editor for that mention. You can change
the linked entity or adjust the text boundaries.

## Adding relations

Switch to the **Relations** panel and click **Add relation**. Select a subject
entity, a predicate, and an object entity. Relations are saved alongside the
entity annotations.

## Completion

When you have finished annotating an article, mark it as **Complete** in the
Summary panel. It then moves to the curation queue.
